WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
David Blumenau. A small tour of things I've built.

00:03.000 --> 00:11.333
A working portfolio comparison switches between two completed generated teapot images.
The original red-handled image is retained beside the mustard revision.

00:11.333 --> 00:14.333
Actual gallery capture: the revision links to its original.

00:14.333 --> 00:16.333
Actual Mac exchange, build121.

00:16.333 --> 00:22.333
Automated Intel Computer Helper selects Session cards
and submits the native Attention answer.

00:22.333 --> 00:28.333
The same actual Codex CLI task receives the returned answer
and acknowledges the selected layout.

00:28.333 --> 00:31.333
A later recorded moment: the resulting three-session workshop page.

00:31.333 --> 00:35.333
Local experiment: the browser closes its response stream mid-answer.

00:35.333 --> 00:42.033
The partial answer freezes while the same engine process continues.
This does not demonstrate a process restart.

00:42.033 --> 00:47.333
The engine stores the answer.
The browser retrieves it and repeats the read.

00:47.333 --> 00:53.333
The working Studio tool gets a new headline
and an amber background. Fictional sample.

00:53.333 --> 00:59.333
The animation is paused and a PNG is downloaded locally.
Studio adapts David's Kitforge renderer.

00:59.333 --> 01:02.333
Actual PNG download.
Its pixels match the paused preview.

01:02.333 --> 01:06.433
World illustrates the same recorded task.
Fixed choice; nothing is sent.

01:06.433 --> 01:11.208
The answer returns; the page unfolds.
Original participant: automated Computer Use.

01:11.208 --> 01:14.200
The actual generated workshop page opens for inspection.

01:14.200 --> 01:18.200
David Blumenau. Explore the work. Borrow the tools.
